Subject: [PATCH 539/539] [DS4.1] mHC's post_pre takes five and six ranks'
 unreduced parts

With sequence-parallel prefill on the rank-order reduce-scatter, a layer
declares post_pre at world = TP size (TileKernelsMHC._entries), and
project_streams asserted world <= 4: at TP5 and TP6 the worker failed while
preparing kernels, before serving anything.

The bound was the rank counts served, not the kernel's. project_streams adds
the parts with `for r in T.unroll(world)`, each a vectorised load of the
thread's COLS columns of X[r] and an FP32 add into the same COLS registers
(the first taken as is), then one rounding: registers and shared memory do
not grow with world, only the unrolled loads. The bound is now the
rank-order sum's, MAX_RANK_ORDER_WORLD (6), so post_pre and RankOrderParts.sum
add the same parts in the same order at every rank count they share.

Worlds 1-4 build the same IR as before (TileLang 0.1.15's get_tir: identical
scripts for pre, broadcast and post_pre at 1-4); worlds 5 and 6 build X as
(world, M, H) with the parts loop unrolled world times. The GPU tests that
compare post_pre and post on unreduced parts with their rank-order sum now
cover five and six parts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
